Subject: [PATCH 09308/11362] Record the goal-defect gate defect: it probes the
 head of a window, the win is at the tail

Found by the 2026-08-18 A/B. `_GOAL_PROBE_MAX_GRIDS = 12` probes the first six
transitions, and every window ends at its level flip, so the win frame is always the
last grid. The win is visible only for windows of six transitions or fewer -- two of the
four games in the A/B are longer. On those, a CORRECT predicate is necessarily
constant-False across everything the gate sees, so the gate rejects correct predicates
and rewards early false positives, on exactly the windows where induction is hardest.

That would only waste a re-ask, except the re-ask is not goal-only. `_split_induce` does
not exist outside comments; the live path is a single combined generate() call and the
goal gate arms on it, so a goal re-ask regenerates the world model too. Function-level
hashes of captured engines differ in 5 of 5 paired cells. In ar25 t0 it turned
cell_recall 1.0 with a defective goal -- which found a real level-up in 15 actions --
into cell_recall 0.0 with a perfect goal, which found nothing.

The flag is default-off, so no live impact today. Recorded because it degrades precisely
the longest-window games, and silently: re-asks fire, the accepted predicate looks
plausible, and the discarded engine is invisible.

The fix is to include the final transition rather than raise the constant, which would
repair the symptom only until a window outgrows the new number.

